<title>UK: Italy's Prodi hopeful of metalworkers deal soon.</title>
<headline>Italy's Prodi hopeful of metalworkers deal soon.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian Prime Minister Romano Prodi said on Friday he was hopeful a solution could be found shortly to end a protracted dispute between employers and Italy's engineering and metalworking industry.</p>
<p>Speaking after talks with British Prime Minister John Major, Prodi told reporters that trades unions and employers were now much closer together.</p>
<p>&quot;I hope we shall soon be in the final straight,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Government-brokered talks between unions and employers resumed this week in a bid to end a lengthy pay dispute which involves some 1.7 million workers. The sector's two-year contract expired in June.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
